# API keys of the VanishingPoint skill (new member page, 2026-10-26)

Every key is **optional**: without a key, the source concerned is skipped or degraded **with a receipt**, never "nothing found" (SKILL.md "What we do not do"). No key value is ever displayed, journaled or written into a URL. To know what you are missing: `python3 -I tools/check_keys.py` (offline; prints, per plugin, the active, degraded and skipped sources with the link to obtain each key); `--announce` returns this text only on the first run and when the set changes (fingerprint of the names in `~/.config/vp/keys-state.json`); `--suggest "<angles>"` proposes (at most 2) a missing free source when the `useful_when:` line of its plugin overlaps the question.

## How the skill reads a key (single rule, `tools/code_sources.py` `key(NAME)`, reused by the gateway and by the GitHub token)

1. Environment variable `NAME` (exact name declared by the plugin); non-empty value -> taken (surrounding whitespace removed).
2. Otherwise the file **`~/.config/vp/<name in lowercase>.key`**, exact name, "_key" included: `OPENALEX_KEY` -> `openalex_key.key`, `NCBI_API_KEY` -> `ncbi_api_key.key`, `VP_GITHUB_TOKEN` -> `vp_github_token.key`, `PISTE_CLIENT_ID` -> `piste_client_id.key`.

An empty or unreadable file = absent; `None` = the source does without. Nothing is required, no value is displayed or journaled. There is no other lookup location: on a machine where keys were kept elsewhere, copy them to `~/.config/vp/`.

The GitHub token (`read_token()`) follows this same rule; it is sent only as `Authorization: Bearer` to `api.github.com`, never on a redirect, and refused (never sent) if it is not printable ASCII of at least 8 characters (`credential_invalid`).

Today only **`OPENALEX_KEY`** (added as `api_key=` to OpenAlex calls) and **`VP_GITHUB_TOKEN`** (GitHub code search) change a network call. `OPENROUTER_API_KEY` is read by `tools/contradictor.py` only (contradictor option, never by the gateway). The others are **declared, with no effect until wired**: `NCBI_API_KEY` and `SWH_TOKEN` (engine wired but key not yet passed through), `S2_API_KEY`, `OPENAIRE_TOKEN`, `FRED_API_KEY`, `PISTE_*` (engine not wired); `check_keys.py` says so on each line concerned.

## Key table (declared in the ```sources blocks of the plugins, or "keyed" options of their text)

| Variable (exact name) | Plugin(s) | What it opens | Free, conditions | Where to obtain it (checked 2026-10-26) | Delay | Installation |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| `OPENALEX_KEY` | biology, cs-ai, law, finance | OpenAlex: daily budget x10, 30 req/s instead of 10; without key, 429 possible -> Crossref fallback reported | Free, nominative account (e-mail) | https://openalex.org/signup then Settings -> API key (doc: https://help.openalex.org/how-to-use-the-api/rate-limits-and-authentication ; `openalex.org/settings/api` returns 403 to robots, open it in a browser) | Immediate (activation link by e-mail) | env `OPENALEX_KEY` or `~/.config/vp/openalex_key.key` |
| `VP_GITHUB_TOKEN` | code | GitHub `search/code` and GraphQL (token required by GitHub); core 5,000 req/h instead of 60; without token: `{"status":"skipped","reason":"credential_missing"}`, Sourcegraph continues | Free, GitHub account; **read-only** (fine-grained, no write permission, public repositories) | https://github.com/settings/tokens (redirects to login) | Immediate | env `VP_GITHUB_TOKEN` or `~/.config/vp/vp_github_token.key` |
| `OPENROUTER_API_KEY` | code (contradictor option, `tools/contradictor.py` only) | OpenRouter: the `kimi` and `gemini` contradictor families only; without key those families are skipped (`credential_missing`); the `codex` (Codex CLI) and `claude` (`claude -p`) families need no key | Paid per call (about 0.26 USD per contradictor call measured); account | https://openrouter.ai/settings/keys | Immediate | `~/.config/vp/openrouter_api_key.key` or the environment variable |
| `NCBI_API_KEY` | biology | PubMed E-utilities: 10 req/s instead of 3 | Free, NCBI account | NCBI account -> Settings -> "API Key Management" (announcement: https://ncbiinsights.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/2017/11/02/new-api-keys-for-the-e-utilities/ ; `account.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov` is behind reCAPTCHA for robots) | Immediate | env `NCBI_API_KEY` or `~/.config/vp/ncbi_api_key.key` -- declared, no effect until wired |
| `S2_API_KEY` | cs-ai | Semantic Scholar: `/paper/search`, `/bulk` search, snippets (429 almost systematic without key); engine **not wired** | Free by form; 1 req/s at first; data CC BY-NC / ODC-BY, attribution, no redistribution | https://www.semanticscholar.org/product/api (form `#api-key-form`) | Key sent by e-mail, reviewed (delay not announced) | env `S2_API_KEY` or `~/.config/vp/s2_api_key.key` |
